-- Static catalog of fishing catches for Dark Matter Show all (generated by tools/catalog/gen_catalog.py).
-- Facts (item id, name, quality, typical waters, skill hint) were researched on public pages and entered here;
-- nothing is copied from another addon's loot tables.
--
-- Item ids: each item's own page on warcraft.wiki.gg (its Wowhead item link), e.g. https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Raw_Longjaw_Mud_Snapper
-- Waters / skill: https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fishing_locations (modern table; skill = lowest '100% catch' zone skill listed, a hint only).
-- Forever: Wowhead Forever (https://www.wowhead.com/forever) refused automated fetches (HTTP 403) and no public Forever
--   fishing loot table or Forever patch note on fishing could be found (https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/World_of_Warcraft:_Forever).
--   So every entry is classicOnly = true (shown only when C_Item.DoesItemExistByID confirms it on this client),
--   except items confirmed on a live Forever 1.60.1 client (caught in Dark Matter 0.2.5, 2026-10-19): forever = true.
-- Excluded as added after Classic per their wiki patch notes: Old Crafty / Old Ironjaw (2.3.0), Stendel's Bane (4.1.0),
--   Driftwood and the other 3.1.0 junk, Steam Pump Debris (2.0.3), Broken Engine Part (2.3.0), Water Snail (10.0.2),
--   Electropeller / Gaffer Jack (4.0.3 quests). 0.2.6 entries with no fishing source (Oozing Bag, Ruined Pelt, Damp Diary
--   Page, Schematic: Field Repair Bot 74A, Dark Iron Ore, Essence of Undeath) were removed. 13888 is Darkclaw Lobster
--   (0.2.6 labelled it Darkshore Grouper, which is 12238).
--
